/-!
# Cohomology over a presheaf of sets

For a ringed site `X` and a presheaf of sets `K` on it, the cohomology of a sheaf of
`O_X`-modules over `K` agrees with the cohomology of its underlying sheaf of abelian groups
over `K`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients.freeModuleSheafOnPresheaf` is the sheaf of modules
  freely generated by a presheaf of sets.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients.modulePresheafCohomologyFunctor` is cohomology over a
  presheaf of sets, computed in sheaves of modules: `Ext` out of the free sheaf of modules.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients.abelianPresheafCohomologyFunctor` is the corresponding
  functor on the underlying abelian sheaves.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients.modulePresheafCohomologyFunctorIso` is
  [Stacks, Tag 079Y]: the two cohomology functors are identified, naturally in the coefficient
  sheaf of modules.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients.freeSheafIsoTensorSheaf` is the input that makes the
  identification possible, and is of independent interest: the sheafified free presheaf of
  `O_X`-modules on `K` is the sheafified extension of scalars along `O_X` of the free abelian
  presheaf on `K`.

## Implementation notes

**Degree by degree, out of one comparison in degree zero.** Both functors are the degree-`p`
part of a `δ`-functor on sheaves of modules — `Ext` out of a fixed object for the first, and
that composed with `SheafOfModules.toSheaf` for the second — and both `δ`-functors are
universal, so by [Stacks, Tag 010U]
(`CategoryTheory.DeltaFunctor.IsUniversal.isoOfIso`) an isomorphism of their degree-zero parts
extends uniquely to every degree. Universality of the first is `Ext`-acyclicity against an
injective object; of the second it is
`ModuleSheafCohomology.ext_eq_zero_of_isTorsionFree`, which applies because the sheafification
of a free abelian presheaf is sectionwise torsion free. In degree zero the comparison is
`ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorSheafHomIso`, the hom-isomorphism of [Stacks, Tag 03FD], read
through `ModuleSheafCohomology.extZeroIsoCoyoneda` on both sides.

**Why `freeSheafIsoTensorSheaf` is needed, and why it is proved by corepresentability.** The
degree-zero comparison is stated about the sheafified extension of scalars of the free abelian
presheaf on `K`, whereas cohomology over `K` is `Ext` out of the sheafified *free presheaf of
modules* on `K`. The two objects are canonically isomorphic, but
`ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf` is `@[no_expose]`: under the module system its body is
absent from the olean, so the objectwise identification `R ⊗_ℤ ℤ[K] = R[K]` cannot be written
down at any transparency, and the characterising equations of the extension of scalars are
necessarily private (a `public` theorem may not unfold a `@[no_expose]` definition, even inside
the same module). What *is* public is the hom-isomorphism. So the isomorphism is obtained from
it: both objects corepresent `N ↦ (K ⟶ N)` on sheaves of modules, the first through the
sheafification and free/forget adjunctions for presheaves of modules, the second through the
hom-isomorphism followed by the sheafification adjunction for abelian presheaves and the
free/forget adjunction for abelian groups whiskered to presheaves
(`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.whiskerRight` applied to `AddCommGrpCat.adj`). The two chains land
on the same presheaf of types, by `rfl`.

The corepresentability is run at the level of bare bijections (`isoOfHomEquiv`), not of additive
isomorphisms: the shared middle term is a hom-set of type-valued presheaves and carries no group
structure, and the object isomorphism is all that is used downstream, so no additivity has to be
proved. Each of the four bijections is an adjunction's `homEquiv` or the component of a natural
isomorphism, so each naturality step is an existing lemma rather than a new proof.

**Universes.** The statement is at `HasExt.{u}`, the `Ext` universe equal to the universe of the
site. `ModuleSheafCohomology.ext_eq_zero_of_isTorsionFree` — the only public form of the
`Ext`-vanishing needed for universality of the abelian-side `δ`-functor; the alternative
derivation uses five private lemmas — is stated at `Ext.{u}`, and
`ModuleSheafCohomology.extZeroIsoCoyoneda` at the `Ext` universe equal to the category's
morphism universe. The specialisation is forced by that vocabulary. It is not a restriction of
content: `HasExt.{w}` for a Grothendieck abelian category with `Type u`-valued hom-sets requires
`u ≤ w`, and the `Ext` universe in both statements is incidental to their proofs, so an upstream
generalisation of those two declarations would recover an arbitrary `Ext` universe here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 079Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 010U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/010U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03AD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03AD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Abelian CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients

attribute [local instance] ModuleSheafCohomology.toSheaf_preservesFiniteColimits

/-- Weak sheafification of abelian presheaves on a small site, from the global instance
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.coefficientSheafification`. It is made a local instance of high priority
so that the definitions below find it rather than the section variable
`[HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]`, and so do not depend on that variable. -/
abbrev hasWeakSheafifyAddCommGrpCat {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) :
    HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  inferInstance

attribute [local instance high] hasWeakSheafifyAddCommGrpCat

section Corepresentation

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u})
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (K : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)

/-- The underlying presheaf of types of a sheaf of `R`-modules. -/
def typePresheaf : SheafOfModules.{u} R ⥤ (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) :=
  (SheafOfModules.forget R ⋙ PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 R.obj)) ⋙
    PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj ⋙
      (Functor.whiskeringRight _ _ _).obj (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u})

/-- Two objects corepresenting `N ↦ (K ⟶ N)` by bijections compatible with composition are
isomorphic. -/
def isoOfHomEquiv {A B : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (eA : ∀ N, (A ⟶ N) ≃ (K ⟶ (typePresheaf R).obj N))
    (eB : ∀ N, (B ⟶ N) ≃ (K ⟶ (typePresheaf R).obj N))
    (hA : ∀ {N N'} (f : A ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ N'),
      eA N' (f ≫ g) = eA N f ≫ (typePresheaf R).map g)
    (hB : ∀ {N N'} (f : B ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ N'),
      eB N' (f ≫ g) = eB N f ≫ (typePresheaf R).map g) :
    A ≅ B where
  hom := (eA B).symm (eB B (𝟙 B))
  inv := (eB A).symm (eA A (𝟙 A))
  hom_inv_id := by
    apply (eA A).injective
    rw [hA, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, ← hB, Category.id_comp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  inv_hom_id := by
    apply (eB B).injective
    rw [hB, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, ← hA, Category.id_comp, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- Morphisms out of the sheafified free presheaf of modules on `K` are maps of presheaves of
types out of `K`: the sheafification adjunction followed by the free/forget adjunction for
presheaves of modules. -/
def freeHomEquiv (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
        ((PresheafOfModules.free R.obj).obj K) ⟶ N) ≃ (K ⟶ (typePresheaf R).obj N) :=
  ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (𝟙 R.obj)).homEquiv _ N).trans
    ((PresheafOfModules.freeAdjunction R.obj).homEquiv K _)

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- `freeHomEquiv` is natural in the target sheaf of modules. -/
lemma freeHomEquiv_comp {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (f : (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
      ((PresheafOfModules.free R.obj).obj K) ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ N') :
    freeHomEquiv R K N' (f ≫ g) = freeHomEquiv R K N f ≫ (typePresheaf R).map g :=
  (congrArg ((PresheafOfModules.freeAdjunction R.obj).homEquiv K _)
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (𝟙 R.obj)).homEquiv_naturality_right
        f g)).trans
    ((PresheafOfModules.freeAdjunction R.obj).homEquiv_naturality_right _ _)

/-- Tag 03FD's hom-isomorphism, read at the level of underlying types. -/
def tensorStep1 (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
        (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf R.obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)) ⟶ N) ≃
      ((presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free) ⟶
        (SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N) :=
  ((forget AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
    ((ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorSheafHomIso J R (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)).app N)).toEquiv

/-- The sheafification adjunction for abelian presheaves. -/
def tensorStep2 (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    ((presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free) ⟶
        (SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N) ≃
      (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free ⟶
        (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N)) :=
  (CategoryTheory.sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).homEquiv _ _

/-- The free/forget adjunction for abelian groups, whiskered to presheaves. -/
def tensorStep3 (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free ⟶
        (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N)) ≃
      (K ⟶ (typePresheaf R).obj N) :=
  (Adjunction.whiskerRight Cᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.adj).homEquiv K _

/-- Morphisms out of the sheafified extension of scalars of the free abelian presheaf on `K`
are also maps of presheaves of types out of `K`. -/
def tensorHomEquiv (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
        (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf R.obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)) ⟶ N) ≃
      (K ⟶ (typePresheaf R).obj N) :=
  (tensorStep1 R K N).trans ((tensorStep2 R K N).trans (tensorStep3 R K N))

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- `tensorStep1` is natural in the target sheaf of modules. -/
lemma tensorStep1_comp {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (f : (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
      (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf R.obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)) ⟶ N)
    (g : N ⟶ N') :
    tensorStep1 R K N' (f ≫ g) =
      tensorStep1 R K N f ≫ (SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map g :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    ((ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorSheafHomIso J R (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)).hom.naturality g) f

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- `tensorStep2` is natural in the target sheaf of modules. -/
lemma tensorStep2_comp {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (y : (presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free) ⟶
      (SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N) (g : N ⟶ N') :
    tensorStep2 R K N' (y ≫ (SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map g) =
      tensorStep2 R K N y ≫
        (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map g) :=
  (CategoryTheory.sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).homEquiv_naturality_right _ _

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- `tensorStep3` is natural in the target sheaf of modules. -/
lemma tensorStep3_comp {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (z : K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free ⟶
      (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).obj N))
    (g : N ⟶ N') :
    tensorStep3 R K N'
        (z ≫ (sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).map ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map g)) =
      tensorStep3 R K N z ≫ (typePresheaf R).map g :=
  (Adjunction.whiskerRight Cᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.adj).homEquiv_naturality_right _ _

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- `tensorHomEquiv` is natural in the target sheaf of modules. -/
lemma tensorHomEquiv_comp {N N' : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (f : (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
      (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf R.obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)) ⟶ N)
    (g : N ⟶ N') :
    tensorHomEquiv R K N' (f ≫ g) =
      tensorHomEquiv R K N f ≫ (typePresheaf R).map g :=
  (congrArg (fun w => tensorStep3 R K N' (tensorStep2 R K N' w))
      (tensorStep1_comp R K f g)).trans
    ((congrArg (tensorStep3 R K N') (tensorStep2_comp R K _ g)).trans
      (tensorStep3_comp R K _ g))

/-- **The free sheaf of modules on `K` is the sheafified extension of scalars along `R` of the
free abelian presheaf on `K`.**  Both corepresent `N ↦ (K ⟶ N)` on sheaves of modules — the
first by the sheafification and free/forget adjunctions for presheaves of modules, the second by
Tag 03FD's hom-isomorphism followed by the sheafification adjunction for abelian presheaves and
the free/forget adjunction for abelian groups — so they agree. -/
def freeSheafIsoTensorSheaf :
    (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj ((PresheafOfModules.free R.obj).obj K) ≅
      (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 R.obj)).obj
        (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf R.obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)) :=
  isoOfHomEquiv R K (freeHomEquiv R K) (tensorHomEquiv R K)
    (fun f g => freeHomEquiv_comp R K f g) (fun f g => tensorHomEquiv_comp R K f g)

end Corepresentation

section Universality

variable (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}) (K : X.Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)

/-- A free abelian group is torsion free, so the free abelian presheaf on `K` is sectionwise
torsion free. -/
lemma isTorsionFree_free (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    Module.IsTorsionFree ℤ ((K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free).obj U) := by
  change Module.IsTorsionFree ℤ (FreeAbelianGroup (K.obj U))
  exact Module.Flat.isTorsionFree

/-- Sheafification preserves sectionwise torsion-freeness, so the sheafification of the free
abelian presheaf on `K` is sectionwise torsion free. -/
lemma isTorsionFree_sheafified (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    Module.IsTorsionFree ℤ
      (((presheafToSheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)).obj.obj U) :=
  ModuleSheafCohomology.isTorsionFree_sheafify X.J (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)
    (isTorsionFree_free X K) U

/-- **The abelian-side `δ`-functor is universal.** `Ext` out of the sheafification of the free
abelian presheaf on `K` vanishes in positive degree against the underlying abelian sheaf of an
injective sheaf of modules, because that sheafification is sectionwise torsion free. -/
lemma universal_target [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u})] :
    (ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
      ((presheafToSheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free))).IsUniversal :=
  ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor_isUniversal _ _ (by
    intro I _ n a
    exact ModuleSheafCohomology.ext_eq_zero_of_isTorsionFree X.J
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) I _ (isTorsionFree_sheafified X K) n a)

/-- **The module-side `δ`-functor is universal.** `Ext` out of any object vanishes in positive
degree against an injective object, and sheaves of modules on a small site have enough
injectives. -/
lemma universal_source
    [HasExt.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))]
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :
    (ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor
      (𝟭 (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) M).IsUniversal :=
  have : EnoughInjectives (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
    SheafOfModules.enoughInjectivesU.{u, u, u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)
  ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor_isUniversal _ M (by
    intro I _ n a
    change Ext M I (n + 1) at a
    exact Ext.eq_zero_of_injective a)

end Universality

section Main

variable (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}) (K : X.Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (p : ℕ)

/-- The sheaf of modules freely generated by a presheaf of sets on a ringed site. -/
@[sga "4 I 7.13" "The object O_X[F]"]
public def freeModuleSheafOnPresheaf :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{u} (𝟙 (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj)).obj
    (PresheafOfModules.freeObj (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj) K)

/-- Cohomology over a presheaf of sets, computed in sheaves of modules. -/
public def modulePresheafCohomologyFunctor
    [HasExt.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))] :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  (extFunctor p).obj (op (freeModuleSheafOnPresheaf X K))

/-- Cohomology over a presheaf of sets after forgetting the module structure on the
coefficient sheaf. -/
public def abelianPresheafCohomologyFunctor [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u})] :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) ⋙
    (extFunctor p).obj (op ((presheafToSheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
      (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free)))

/-- The sheafified extension of scalars along `O_X` of the free abelian presheaf on `K`. -/
def tensorModuleSheaf : SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj)).obj
    (ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorPresheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj
      (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free))

/-- **The comparison in degree zero.** `Ext` in degree zero out of an object is the
corepresentable functor it determines (`ModuleSheafCohomology.extZeroIsoCoyoneda`), and the two
corepresentable functors in question are identified by the hom-isomorphism of Tag 03FD. -/
def degreeZeroIso [HasExt.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))]
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u})] :
    (ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor
        (𝟭 (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
        (tensorModuleSheaf X K)).functor 0 ≅
      (ModuleSheafCohomology.extDeltaFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        ((presheafToSheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
          (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free))).functor 0 :=
  Functor.leftUnitor _ ≪≫ ModuleSheafCohomology.extZeroIsoCoyoneda _ ≪≫
    ModuleSheafCohomology.tensorSheafHomIso X.J (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)
      (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free) ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
      (ModuleSheafCohomology.extZeroIsoCoyoneda _).symm

/-- The comparison of the two `δ`-functors, in degree `p`: both are universal and their
degree-zero parts are identified by `degreeZeroIso`, so Stacks 010U extends that identification
to every degree. -/
def comparison [HasExt.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))]
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u})] :
    (extFunctor p).obj (op (tensorModuleSheaf X K)) ≅
      SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) ⋙
        (extFunctor p).obj (op ((presheafToSheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
          (K ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.free))) :=
  haveI := universal_source X (tensorModuleSheaf X K)
  haveI := universal_target X K
  letI d := DeltaFunctor.IsUniversal.isoOfIso (degreeZeroIso X K)
  (Functor.leftUnitor _).symm ≪≫
    { hom := d.hom.app p
      inv := d.inv.app p
      hom_inv_id := congrArg (fun η => η.app p) d.hom_inv_id
      inv_hom_id := congrArg (fun η => η.app p) d.inv_hom_id }

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 079Y.** Cohomology of a sheaf of modules over a presheaf of sets is
canonically and naturally isomorphic to the cohomology of its underlying sheaf of abelian
groups. -/
@[stacks 079Y, sga "4 V 3.5" "H^q isomorphisms", sga "4 V 2.3.6" "e)", sga "4 V 4.4"]
public def modulePresheafCohomologyFunctorIso
    [HasExt.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))]
    [HasExt.{u} (Sheaf X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u})] :
    modulePresheafCohomologyFunctor X K p ≅ abelianPresheafCohomologyFunctor X K p :=
  ((extFunctor p).mapIso
      (freeSheafIsoTensorSheaf (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) K).op).symm ≪≫
    comparison X K p

end Main

end Stacks.Cohomology.PresheafCoefficients

end
